From e7c1d2a454824ab6df6cf56115bfb33e0f081060 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:26:01 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Bluetooth: SMP: distribute local identity for LE legacy
 OOB bonds

The kernel only offers SMP_DIST_ID_KEY - our IRK and Identity Address -
when HCI_PRIVACY is enabled.  The peripherals that need LE legacy OOB
expect it unconditionally: they only commit the bond to flash after the
initiator has sent Identity Information and Identity Address Information
in phase 3.  Without those PDUs the Microsoft Modern Keyboard (model
1780) completes pairing, stores nothing, and never reconnects - the bond
exists on the host side only.

Add SMP_DIST_ID_KEY to the local key distribution when an LE legacy OOB
Temporary Key is armed for the peer.  This is scoped to exactly the
pairings the previous patch already forces to legacy OOB, so no other
pairing starts distributing an identity it did not before, and the peer
still decides what it actually asks for in its Pairing Response.

Signed-off-by: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/smp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/smp.c b/net/bluetooth/smp.c
index 6bb9d3b4f..2c2350653 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/smp.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/smp.c
@@ -676,10 +676,18 @@ static void build_pairing_cmd(struct l2cap_conn *conn,
 	 * have OOB data.  An SC-capable adapter has SMP_AUTH_SC set here and
 	 * would otherwise take the Secure Connections OOB path below, which
 	 * needs P-256 confirm/random values the peer does not have.
+	 *
+	 * Also offer SMP_DIST_ID_KEY so we distribute our IRK and Identity
+	 * Address in phase 3.  Peripherals in this class only commit the bond
+	 * to flash once the initiator has sent Identity Information and
+	 * Identity Address Information; without them the bond exists on our
+	 * side only and the device never reconnects.  The kernel otherwise
+	 * offers the local identity only under HCI_PRIVACY.
 	 */
 	if (smp_le_legacy_oob_data(hcon)) {
 		authreq &= ~SMP_AUTH_SC;
 		oob_flag = SMP_OOB_PRESENT;
+		local_dist |= SMP_DIST_ID_KEY;
 	}
 
 	if (hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_SC_ENABLED) &&
